 "short_name": "Dihlabeng",
 "_doc": "Free State ledger bill, same print family as mangaung / overstrand / maluti (ACCOUNT NO: + street on one line, DEPOSIT DATE header block, 'TAX INVOICE (VAT REG. NO.:nnnn)', DETAILS/DATE/REFERENCE/AMOUNT ledger, '120 + DAYS' ageing row, per-service summary block bottom-right). Dihlabeng's own VAT reg is 4000846529 - that is the fingerprint. NOTE: these PDFs carry [address removed] (and one carries [address removed]), which is why they used to hijack the mangaung profile; never fingerprint on the CBRE recipient address. LAYOUT: (1) the two dates in the meter-table header line 'TYPE  METER NUMBER  YYYY/MM/DD  YYYY/MM/DD' ARE the period start/end - there is no other period print. (2) Meter rows are 'EL <meter> <prev> <new> <consumed> <tariffcode> 0+ @ <rate>'. Rows whose rate is 0.0* are the no-charge sub-meter (ledger line 'ELEC NO CHARGE ME03(NOT APPLICABLE)'); they are captured separately (dih_nc_*) and kept OUT of the canonical kWh/reading columns. Billed row: consumed x rate == the ledger charge to the cent on 11 of 12 bills (DIH_JUN 25 spans the 1-July tariff change so the printed rate is the new one only). new-prev == consumed on all 12. (3) The electricity charge is the ledger line whose REFERENCE column holds the elec meter number ('INDUSTRIAL<500 KVA(BELOW)' on this account) - matched structurally (DETAILS / date / numeric reference / amount, excluding BALANCE B/FWD, RECEIPT and ELEC NO CHARGE) so a different tariff description still works. That description is used as Tariff Name. (4) '** VAT **' is ONE VAT figure for the whole bill (electricity + sundry), not a per-service VAT, so there is no ex/inc split per service in the ledger. (5) The bottom-right summary block prints RATES/SANIT/WATER/REFUSE/SUNDRY/ELECT/REST/TOTAL with SEQUENCE/CURRENT/AMOUNT DUE columns; 'ELECT' there is INCLUSIVE of VAT (ELECT == elec ex-VAT x 1.15 to the cent on all 11 normally-issued bills) so it is NOT mapped into any canonical Rand column - it is kept as dih_sum_elect_r and used as the independent identity check. (6) The bill is single-band: one energy charge, no TOU, no demand, no NMD, no Actual/Estimate flag -> those canonical columns are '_none'. (7) [number removed].pdf is a REPRINT (Nov-2025 period, tax invoice no dated 2026/07/21, recipient DIANAB@ instead of gyro_utilities@): its ledger is real but the summary block and the ageing CURRENT column were re-rendered as 0.00/0.01, so summary-derived identities do not hold on that one file. That is why total_ex_vat_r is taken from the ledger charge lines, not from the summary. (8) Water/sanitation/refuse are 0.00 on every bill of this account and print no meter or ledger line, so no water/sewerage/refuse sections are defined; the summary-block figures are still captured at document scope (dih_sum_water_r etc.) so a future Dihlabeng account with water shows up immediately.",
